{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "138",
 "name": "Asketi's Mount",
 "file": "Map138_Asketis_Mount.xml",
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":40,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Dirge's Solace, Garden of Souls","descriptions":["Blue icicles cascade down the walls onto the white drifts of frost covering the floor.  Carved from grey ice, a banshee clad in a tattered funereal shroud stands with her head thrown back in a soundless wail while snow adders writhe about her feet.  The tinkling of shattering ice is accompanied by the eerie fluting of the winds directed by holes drilled into the cavern walls.  A carved granite door is set in one cavern wall, leading deeper into the mountain."],"exits":[{"to":3,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":2,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":2,"x":20,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Adder's Nest, Frozen Tunnels","descriptions":["Recessed into an arched alcove is a granite door embedded with a softly glowing crystal.  The lintel of the arch is skillfully carved with a fancifully rendered sunburst, although a thick layer of frost makes it difficult to ascertain the details.  Even the suggestion of warmth from a graven image is ruthlessly smothered by the icy cold."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":1,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF","linksTo":"Map139_Adders_Nest.xml"},
  {"id":3,"x":60,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Dirge's Solace, Garden of Souls","descriptions":["Light creeps in from the enormous gash that leads into the cavern, illuminating the chill vapors clinging to the floor with a diffuse glow.  Dripping from the ceiling like the stalactites of more conventional caves, massive icicles catch and reflect the light in a sparkling display.  The tinkling of cracking ice provides a staccato counterpoint to the moaning of the wind whipping through the entry."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":4,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":4,"x":60,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Gate of Souls","descriptions":["Three blackened granite spires rise up out of the ground to form a stunning gateway leading into the gaping maw of a large cave.  The fog that so heavily dominates this side of the mountain's summit recoils from the frigid blasts of air that emanate from within as if they were the expelled breath of Asketi herself."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":5,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":3,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":5,"x":40,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The winding path continues to meander its way around the impressive temple.  The frigid temperatures bite to the very core of one's being, sapping the will to continue.  A light fog lingers in this slightly lower area of the mountain's summit, creeping eerily over the ground without direction like a ghostly apparition."],"exits":[{"to":4,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":6,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":6,"x":20,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A miniature shrine, if it could even be called that, rests dangerously close to the summit's edge.  Sheltered inside the shrine is a diminutive representation of a withered, grey hag bearing a rough burlap sack at her hip and a blood-stained scythe in her right hand that is poised for a strike above her head.  Propped at the base of the figure is a badly weathered crib filled with rotten vegetables that have been preserved only by the sheer lack of warmth to be found here atop the world."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":7,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":7,"x":0,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A small twig has been forcefully shoved into a rounded mound of ice.  A tiny, faded ribbon that desperately clings to the twig holds a broken medallion fluttering in the moaning winds.  Etched upon the half of the medallion that remains is the broad head of what once would have been an impressive unicorn.  A single ice crystal has frozen just under the unicorn's eye, as if it were a tear of sadness from the avatar's goddess."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":8,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":8,"x":-20,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A haunting yet melodic whisper is carried on the wind as it gusts through the trees of the forests below.  In the brief reprieves from the vigorous gales, a thin, lingering fog wavers in and out of view just inches above the ice and rubble-covered ground."],"exits":[{"to":7,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":9,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":9,"x":-40,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The looming temple partly shadows the surface during the morning hours of the day.  Even when the sun gazes down fully upon Elanthia from its throne at midday, shadows manage to creep westward from some of the more prominent spires of the temple.  As day descends into night, though, the shadows hastily retreat into the mica-flecked granite of the mighty fortress, patiently waiting for the time to creep out into the world again."],"exits":[{"to":8,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":10,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":10,"x":-60,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["When not blanketed with clouds, the sky remains a brilliant whitish blue throughout all but the final moments of the day.  In these uncharacteristically beautiful moments, deep purples and blues intermix with vibrant and fiery reds and oranges upon the sky's vast canvas.  A stone bench, which is new compared to the temple itself, rests midway between the temple and the summit's edge for those desiring to gaze upon the sight."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":11,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":11,"x":-60,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Some rocks have obviously been moved from their natural resting places into an arrow-like formation.  A rough, uneven mound of snow provides an incline for the southward-pointing arrow to rest upon.  Throughout most of the year the object being pointed to remains a mystery.  However, those lucky enough to catch the first light of dawn through the spring and summer will find the arrow pointing to the Adder constellation low on the southern horizon."],"exits":[{"to":10,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":12,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":12,"x":-40,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The crippling blight that plagues the region emanates outward from the majestic Temple of the North Wind.  For as far as the eye can see towards the southwest the typically vibrant colors of the trees and other native foliage are dulled throughout the year.  In place of spring greens and autumn reds and oranges are muted olives and browns.  Even the white of snow-capped trees lower on the mountain is dingy and impure."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":11,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":13,"x":-20,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Unlike the rubble-riddled ground near the temple, the mountain's surface becomes smooth and relatively free of debris save for dark swirls that wind their way through the frozen snow and ice towards the southern edge.  The surrounding ice is lessened by the swirls, sapped of its luster and purity.  Two boulders lean against one another near the massive granite structure, a narrow crevice remaining between the boulders and the ground beneath them."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":12,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":14,"x":0,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Countless decades of fierce winds have worn the ground completely smooth.  The light rubble that dots a few small patches of the ice's surface is only discernable from the mixed snow and ice in some areas by its light discoloration under the surface."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":13,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":15,"x":0,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The only evidence of a seasonal melt of the snow and ice is a worn crevice in the rock that slants ever more steeply towards the blighted lands around Asketi's mountain.  Little more than a trickle ever makes its journey downwards at any given time, though the years of the slow moving liquids have gradually eroded the ground to form the crevice."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":16,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":16,"x":20,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The darkened temple towers over the barren landscape, yet still the bone-chilling winds shriek wildly all about as if the temple were no deterrent at all to their ferocity.  Loose rubble shifts dangerously loudly with each step taken.  Jagged pillars of ice have been eternally frozen in a desperate grasp toward the heavens above.","Even the looming temple is not enough of a barrier to stifle the bone-chilling winds that claim dominance in this barren, frozen place.  Great pillars of jagged, ageless ice reach skyward as if they were massive hands seeking affirmation of life beyond the temple's great shadows."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":17,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":15,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":17,"x":40,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Plunging downwards in a near-vertical drop, a sheer granite cliff forms the southern face of the mountain's summit.  Thin, wispy clouds writhe about the summit, sometimes taking the form of ground-hugging fog and other times swirling through the wild currents of wind like ghoulish apparitions.","Plunging downwards in a near-vertical drop, a sheer granite cliff forms the southern face of the mountain's summit.  To the north, like a spear thrust into the heart of a large beast, the mountain reaches higher and higher to pierce the very heavens.  Serpentine columns sculpted into the hard rock spiral about a massive structure carved into the solid rock of the mountaintop."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":16,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":31,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":18,"x":40,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Temple of the North Wind","descriptions":["Asketi's immaculate Temple of the North Wind towers above the flat summit, further dwarfing everything in the surrounding countryside.  Carved directly from the granite mountain, the strength and security of the structure is unquestionable.  Small ice crystals carried on the wind's updraft have coalesced to form a thin layer of frost on the temple's surface.  Twisted shadows race across the granite arch entrance, but in the absence of light, it's hard to discern whether the shadows are real or imagined.","Asketi's immaculate Temple of the North Wind towers above the flat summit, further dwarfing everything in the surrounding countryside.  Carved directly from the granite mountain itself, the strength and security of the structure is unquestionable.  Small flecks of mica scattered throughout the structure glint softly in the day's light.  Great black spires, reminiscent of twining adders, twist and wrap about one another as they climb ever higher, casting foreboding shadows upon the temple's entrance arch."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":17,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":16,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":32,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":19,"x":60,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Frozen shards of stone and ice form a fine, loose rubble over the ground.  Asketi's frozen North Wind shrieks out from around the temple and plummets over the edge of the lifeless mountaintop.  For those brave enough to look, a vast view of the surrounding lands stretches out as far as the eye can see.  Dark shadows blanket the forests below.  The bowing of the trees to the force of the winds gives the illusion of shadowy phantasms sweeping over the countryside.","Frozen shards of stone and ice form a fine, loose rubble over the ground.  Asketi's frozen North Wind shrieks out from around the temple and plummets over the edge of the lifeless mountaintop.  For those brave enough to look, a vast, uninterrupted view of the surrounding forests stretches out as far as the eye can see.  Grey, withered trees stand sentry near the base of the mountain while those still bearing signs of health stretch skyward further away."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":17,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":18,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":20,"x":60,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Unnaturally long shadows flit about the darkened area, though where the shadows' owners may be can only be left to speculation.  A solid sheet of ice blankets the ground here, freezing the rubble firmly into place.  The ice is mostly smooth and unmarred except where broken shards of rubble rest.","Most of the ground is solid ice, as if a small stream of water had somehow erupted from the depths of the mountain and fallen prey to the wicked winds.  The rubble here has been frozen firmly into place and makes little noise beneath the moving feet of those who dare travel the region."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":21,"x":80,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A serpentine column of ice twists and winds its way across the ground before arching up into the air.  A frozen, dark substance runs the length of the ice, contained almost precisely within the center of the structure.  An enigma in both form and purpose, the frozen mass is remarkably free of the gravelly debris present even on the very ground that supports the column."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":20,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":22,"x":100,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A small scrap of cloth has been half-frozen into the disheveled rubble and ice mixture.  The wild winds have blown the scrap into little more than tattered shreds of the garment to which it used to belong.  A single red stripe on the cloth's underside remains untouched by the harsh climate, seemingly a testament to hope not being entirely forsaken in these troubled lands."],"exits":[{"to":23,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":21,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":23,"x":100,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The winds screech angrily about as a corner of the temple deflects their hurried course.  The dark granite structure has been worn smooth with the passage of both wind and time alike.  Rather than snowdrifts filling the wind-guarded niche, an angled mound of solid ice studded with bits of stone climbs the temple's surface."],"exits":[{"to":24,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":22,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":24,"x":120,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Twin statues stand guard here, each gazing out upon the tainted lands surrounding the mountain.  Both statues have been carved from very fine obsidian, obviously not native to the mountaintop, and both resemble Asketi's black unicorns.  While one peers northeasterly towards the wholesome lands of Therengia far off in the distance, the other scrutinizes the lands of Zoluren and even Ilithi to the southeast.  A cool, gentle fog writhes about the two figures."],"exits":[{"to":25,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":23,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":25,"x":140,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Wraithlike wisps of thick fog blanket the side of the mountain and roll listlessly over the summit's edge.  As if the tendrils of fog weren't ominous enough, as each moon rises and shines its light upon the area, the fog fully takes on the lunar body's haunting glow.","Wraithlike wisps of thick fog blanket the side of the mountain and roll listlessly over the summit's edge.  Rather than dissipating into the swift currents of the mountain's winds, the wisps roll out to form a shroud around the face of the mountain against the day's morning sun.  Only during the peak of the sun's journey towards night is the veil pierced and the area illuminated."],"exits":[{"to":24,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":26,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":26,"x":140,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Deep, rolling masses of spectral fog creep in and continue on over the mountain's edge.  Though the writhing mass is dense, the fog only comes up knee-high on a Human.  Still, each step is dangerous enough to be tested lest some poor soul join the fog in its flight over the mountain's ledge!"],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":25,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":27,"x":120,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Entombed within an area of the ice unmarred by the rocky debris are the remnants of some long-forgotten plant.  Perhaps in a much earlier time such plants were more prevalent here at the top of the world, or perhaps the pitiful thing is all that remains of someone's attempt to deny the brutal savagery of the unforgiving climate."],"exits":[{"to":26,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":28,"x":100,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["Drawn-out shadows stretch wildly across the northern face of the granite structure and leap completely over the mountain's cliff-like ledge.  No fewer than six black marble gargoyles are in sight down the northern face of the temple, each displaying vengeful glowers as they peer out hauntingly in the dim light of night.","The temple's northern face looms above a series of massive statues.  Each statue is a black marble gargoyle captured in some moment of ferocity.  Expressions of rage, lust for battle, and savagery are spread across their faces.  Great taloned claws rake menacingly at the air while several of the statues sport widely spread wings.  The stalwart defenders have stood as guards for countless ages and show no signs of leaving their posts."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":27,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":29,"x":100,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["The scattered debris of a fire lies near a grouping of three large boulders.  The tips of only a few branches show any signs of ever being touched by a flame's life-giving warmth.  Half-buried in a mound of snow and ice is a dulled sphere with a very faint yellow tinge to it, similar to that of a fading favor orb."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":30,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":30,"x":80,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Summit","descriptions":["A delicate fog hugs the ground with its ethereal tendrils, winding its way in and out of the larger rocks that dot the summit's surface.  Errant wisps of the grey substance occasionally spiral upward several feet above the ground.  The hiss of the winds as they blast through tiny holes in the rocks lends the illusion of great, hulking adders keeping a watchful gaze over the area."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":4,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":31,"x":80,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Asketi's Mount, Treacherous Cliff","descriptions":["Dense clouds obscure the view below, while an incredibly steep cliff soars out of sight into the icy mists overhead.  At eye level are slippery mountain walls, marred with craggy holes left by pitons and gouges left by ice axes.  Whistling winds rush down from the summit, trailing plumes of frost crystals that threaten to freeze the breath in one's lungs."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF","linksTo":"Map137_Hags_Crag.xml"},
  {"id":32,"x":40,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Broad Steps","descriptions":["Chiseled from the mountain's bedrock, broad steps faced with marble tile ascend through several feet of solid black granite.  Polished to a soft gleam and carved to resemble undulating adders, ornate silverwillow banisters flow up the walls from the entry arch to the temple above."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":18,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":33,"x":40,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Rows of tall pillars stretch off in either direction, forming a colonnade around the perimeter of the temple's lowest tier.  Standing at the top of a flight of broad steps, a silent figure of cold stone scrutinizes all who ascend."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":44,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":32,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":34,"x":60,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Scandalous by conservative standards, a frieze honoring Kerenhappuch and Idon covers much of the black granite wall.  Icicles reach down the grooves of the fluted pillars, spilling onto the floor and trickling over the edge where the floor ends abruptly.  A pair of marble gargoyles peer over the ledge, as if keeping watch for any foolish enough to attempt scaling the temple wall."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":33,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":35,"x":80,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Nothing but wide-set pillars stands between the open air and the dubious safety of the windswept gallery.  The ledge beyond the columns drops away sheer, plunging into the mists shrouding the base of the temple.  Freezing gusts of wind quickly numb any exposed skin.  Black granite soars overhead, carved with a frieze of malicious gremlins."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":34,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":36,"x":100,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Turning sharply here, the broad ledge of the lower tier is lined with columns sculpted to resemble coiled adders.  The stone serpents overlook the mists rising from the glacial fields below.  A broad staircase has been chiseled into the heavy rock, ascending to the temple's second tier.  Carvings cover the walls on either side of the stairs."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":37,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":45,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":37,"x":80,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Intricately carved friezes depict natural disasters and the aftermath of devastation.  Bitterly cold wind swirls between the granite pillars, exceptionally strong gusts rattling the slender spires as if to underscore the tale of destruction told by the graven images."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":38,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":38,"x":60,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Soaring spires form a wall of sorts along the brink of the precipice.  Like vigilant sentinels, misshapen marble beasts sculpted in wary attitudes crouch between the columns.  One statue, carved in the likeness of a winged orc, regards the frieze opposite him with a supercilious smile."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":39,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":39,"x":40,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Last Sacrifice","descriptions":["Facing directly north, this corner of the temple has neither columns nor statuary to offer shelter from the deadly cold winds.  Close to the ledge stands an angled slab of granite.  Thick frost coats the iron manacles set into the slab, although the dark stone itself is free of rime."],"exits":[{"to":38,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":40,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":40,"x":20,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Featureless stone columns, each polished so perfectly smooth that their curves gleam like a dull mirror, line the broad ledge that makes up the temple's bottom tier.  Speckled with frost, the wall is covered with a frieze carved in high relief."],"exits":[{"to":39,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":41,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":41,"x":0,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Carved in bas-relief, a frieze detailing elaborate scenes of agony and torture covers the wall.  Arctic winds howl around the slim spires thrusting into the sky like spears of stone.  Stinging particles of ice carried by the wind find their way into clothing and armor to produce a bone-deep chill."],"exits":[{"to":40,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":42,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":42,"x":-20,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["The drop beyond the soaring columns is sheer, a vertical buttress cleaving vacant air.  A cold wind whistles around the spires, plucking at hair and clothing like malevolent imps.  Carved into solid granite, a narrow stairway ascends to the temple's second level.  A large sculpture in the middle of the gallery commands attention."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":43,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":49,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":43,"x":0,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Built to honor Asketi, Mistress of the North Wind, the lower tier of the temple is open to the air.  Scoured clean by the relentless wind, twisted monoliths rise dramatically from the outer ledge of the floor.  Only the bulk of the temple's second level provides a modicum of shelter from the icy blasts of air shrieking across the mountain's peak.  A meticulously carved frieze spans the foundation wall of the upper story."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":42,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":44,"x":20,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Colonnade","descriptions":["Giant adders of black granite form the pillars along this stretch of the gallery.  The floor ends just beyond the western side of the columns, dropping a dizzying height to the peak below.  Life-sized statues are displayed on low pedestals situated between the pillars.  Stretching high overhead, a large frieze depicting Dergati graces the eastern wall."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":43,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":45,"x":80,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["This expanse of ground is perfectly flat, as if the mountain's topmost peak had been sliced away.  Rising up out of the snow is a mammoth stone edifice that spans almost the entire length and breadth of the summit.  Glittering with touches of frost, giant columns of black marble support the roof and leave the temple open to the winds.  To the east, a broad staircase cut into the rock leads down."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":46,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":36,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":46,"x":60,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["Gargantuan pillars of hewn stone support a vast roof high overhead.  Bluish light emanates from glowing crystals set in iron sconces affixed to the mighty columns.  Polished smooth as glass, the glossy floor of silver-veined black marble reflects the glow back in pools and arcs that slither across the stone like living things."],"exits":[{"to":45,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":47,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":52,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#00FF00"},
  {"id":47,"x":40,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, High Altar","descriptions":["Open to the elements on all sides, the chamber's only shelter is offered by a roof of stone supported by four pillars.  The seamless flow of granite from the floor to the ceiling bears silent witness that the temple had been hollowed out of the mountain's summit in some long-ago age.  Numerous bones are suspended from the ceiling by slender ropes of steelsilk.  An unadorned altar of ice-blue marble stands in the center of the room, a stark splash of color against the setting of black stone and ivory bone."],"exits":[{"to":46,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":51,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":48,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":50,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Asketi","Altar"]},
  {"id":48,"x":20,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["Gargantuan pillars of hewn stone support a vast roof high overhead.  Bluish light emanates from glowing crystals set in iron sconces affixed to the mighty columns.  Polished smooth as glass, the glossy floor of silver-veined black marble reflects the glow back in pools and arcs that slither across the stone like living things."],"exits":[{"to":47,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":49,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":54,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":49,"x":0,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["This expanse of ground is perfectly flat, as if the mountain's topmost peak had been sliced away.  Rising up out of the snow is a mammoth stone edifice that spans almost the entire length and breadth of the summit.  Glittering with touches of frost, giant columns of black marble support the roof and leave the temple open to the winds.  To the west, a narrow staircase cut into the rock leads down."],"exits":[{"to":50,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":48,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":42,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":50,"x":20,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["Gargantuan pillars of hewn stone support a vast roof high overhead.  Bluish light emanates from glowing crystals set in iron sconces affixed to the mighty columns.  Polished smooth as glass, the glossy floor of silver-veined black marble reflects the glow back in pools and arcs that slither across the stone like living things."],"exits":[{"to":47,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":49,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":51,"x":60,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Dark Sanctuary","descriptions":["Gargantuan pillars of hewn stone support a vast roof high overhead.  Bluish light emanates from glowing crystals set in iron sconces affixed to the mighty columns.  Polished smooth as glass, the glossy floor of silver-veined black marble reflects the glow back in pools and arcs that slither across the stone like living things."],"exits":[{"to":45,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":47,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":55,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#00FF00"},
  {"id":52,"x":40,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Secret Staircase","descriptions":["Featureless black granite walls are polished perfectly so that their smooth curves gleam like a dull mirror.  Four silver sconces set equidistant around the circular chamber provide excellent light.  Shallow steps run along the walls, gradually spiraling downward in a great winding arc.  In the center of the chamber a gaping pit descends into the bedrock.  A silken net hangs from a system of ropes and pulleys affixed by the top of the steps."],"exits":[{"to":53,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":46,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":53,"x":40,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Catacombs","descriptions":["Ascending into shadows above, a staircase follows the walls of the circular chamber.  A low bier covered with black silk stands centered beneath the well formed by the spiraling stairs.  Fitful light cast by lanterns flanking the arch to the north does little to alleviate the darkness closing all around."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF","linksTo":"Map140_Catacombs.xml"},
  {"id":54,"x":20,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, High Priestess' Sanctum","descriptions":["Walls of black marble streaked with ice-blue enclose the circular chamber.  A heavy armchair upholstered in midnight-blue velvet sits behind an intricately carved ebony desk.  Blue silk tassels and fine blue fringe adorn the dark velvet draperies covering most of walls.  Heightening the dramatic darkness of the room by way of contrast, a swirling iridescent cloud hovers against one wall like a mist-filled door."],"exits":[{"to":48,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":55,"x":60,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Temple of the North Wind, Passageway","descriptions":["Darkness here so intense that it is suffocating, relieved only by tiny clusters of glowing bluish crystals clustered along the route.  A swirling iridescent cloud partially juts from a granite wall, its colors bright but producing little light."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":57,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":56,"x":60,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Pilgrimage Trail, The Vela'Tohr Feltery","descriptions":["This cellar is packed almost to the bursting point with various supplies.  Smoked goat and boar hang from the rafters.  Crocks of honey and wheels of goat cheese fill the shelves.  A path winds between barrels of cornmeal and kegs of salt, ending before a dark tunnel.  Necessities like blankets and simple tools, as well as wicker bins filled with potatoes and dried beans, are stacked near the tunnel.  Dusty crates provide access to a swirling iridescent cloud in the ceiling."],"exits":[{"to":57,"exit":"go","move":""},{"to":58,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":57,"x":60,"y":160,"z":1,"title":"A Twisting Tunnel","descriptions":["Fitful flickers of blue light here and there only intensify the darkness of the subterranean passage, providing barely enough illumination to see a scant arm's length ahead."],"exits":[],"color":"#FFFFFF"},
  {"id":58,"x":60,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Pilgrimage Trail, The Vela'Tohr Feltery","descriptions":["The warm glow of oil lamps reveals a spacious hall.  Looms take up the central portion of the space, comfortable padded benches pulled up at each one.  Along the walls, cedar shelves are filled with orderly rows of baskets overflowing with balls of yarn.  Sacks of carded wool, ready to be spun, sit between a pair of spinning wheels positioned next to the dark windows.","Woven mats of sweet grass cover the floor of the spacious hall.  Looms take up the central portion of the space, comfortable padded benches pulled up at each one.  Along the walls, cedar shelves are filled with orderly rows of baskets overflowing with balls of yarn in hues of grey, cream and sable.  Sacks of carded wool, ready to be spun, sit between a pair of spinning wheels positioned next to the large windows facing north."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"go","move":""}],"color":"#FFFFFF","linksTo":"Map129_Pilgramage_Trail.xml"}
 ],
 "labels": [
  {"text":"Black Marble Gargoyle","x":-80,"y":10,"z":0},
  {"text":"Black Marble Gargoyle","x":-80,"y":230,"z":0},
  {"text":"High Priestess'","x":-50,"y":120,"z":1},
  {"text":"Sanctum","x":-40,"y":130,"z":1},
  {"text":"Passage to","x":70,"y":150,"z":1},
  {"text":"Feltery","x":70,"y":160,"z":1}
 ]
}
